Start the program.
Read the number of buildings and pathways.
Initialize the adjacency matrix with zeros.
Accept the pathway connections and update the matrix with 1 for each connection.
Display a menu containing the available operations.
If the user selects Add Building:
Increase the number of buildings by one.
Initialize the new row and column with zeros.
Accept connections to existing buildings.
Update the adjacency matrix.
If the user selects Remove Pathway:
Accept the two building numbers.
Set the corresponding matrix entries to 0.
Display the updated adjacency matrix.
If the user selects Calculate Degree:
Add all the values in each row of the adjacency matrix.
Display the degree of each building.
Repeat the menu until the user selects Exit.
Stop the program.
